# analysis harness artifacts (regenerate from gen_test_signal.py; never commit captures)
*.wav
__pycache__/
.venv/
analysis/pedal_results*/
# Generated A/B report data + per-capture result cache (regenerate via comprehensive_report.py;
# the tracked analysis/reports/*.example.* files are the committed samples)
analysis/reports/comprehensive_data*.json
analysis/reports/cache/
# Per-session scratch reports from --out (candidate scans, A/B pairs). These are
# regenerable and large (~580 KB each; a single session's cap scan is easily 15 MB),
# so they must never be committed. Session 22 widened the line above from an exact
# filename to a glob for the same reason; --out lands OUTSIDE that glob, so match the
# session-tag convention explicitly.
analysis/reports/s[0-9][0-9]_*.json
# ⚠ session 114: the glob above is TWO digits, so every report from session 100 onward (~53 MB by
# s114) silently fell outside it and showed up as untracked. Three-digit sessions, same rule.
analysis/reports/s[0-9][0-9][0-9]_*.json
analysis/reports/s[0-9][0-9][0-9]_*/
# ...and the stdout logs those background renders are launched with (session 49;
# `python3 -u ... > analysis/reports/sNN_*.log`, per the session-43 buffering note).
analysis/reports/s[0-9][0-9]_*.log
analysis/reports/s[0-9][0-9][0-9]_*.log
# ...and the render logs moved to their own directory at some point without the ignore following.
analysis/fit_logs/

# Generated schematic rasters (regenerate via schematics/crop.py; sources are PDFs)
schematics/*.png
